# Read by two flows: the DVSim veriblelint target, which is passed this file through the core, and
# the CI lint job, which concatenates every waiver in the tree into one file. Because of the second,
# anchor a location whenever the rule should only be waived for this top.

# The DUT generate block has to be labelled "dut", because topgen bakes the hierarchy
# tb.dut.top_peppermint.* into the RAL backdoor roots, tb__xbar_connect.sv and the toggle-coverage
# exclusions. A gen_ prefix would break every one of those generated files.
# TODO: remove this waiver along with the generate block once Peppermint has a chip-level wrapper,
#   which satisfies the same hierarchy contract with a named instance (peppermint-embargoed#38).
waive --rule=generate-label-prefix --location=".*top_peppermint/dv/tb/tb\.sv"

# These lines are too long due to templating. Duplicates common.vbl on purpose, as the sibling tops
# do: the DV cores do not depend on lowrisc:lint:common, so common.vbl does not reach the DVSim
# veriblelint target.
#
# Deliberately NOT anchored to this top, so do not "fix" it to match the waiver above. The target is
# ralgen output, which only ever exists inside a build directory, so an anchor could only match the
# scratch path. No ral_pkg under hw/top_peppermint is checked in for one to bite on.
waive --rule=line-length --location=".*ral_pkg.*"
